GIMP Palette
Name: TowerDefense — Verdant Siege
Columns: 4
#
# Direction: a summer hillside with a road cut through it and something coming
# up the road. Storybook rather than grim — the towers are masonry, the grass
# is grass, and the threat is the only thing that looks wrong.
#
# The palette is organised around the one question the player asks every frame:
# can I build here? turf-* is buildable, path-* is not, and they are separated
# by hue (green vs brown) *and* by value, so the grid reads without a single
# gridline drawn over it.
#
# foe-* is warm red-orange, which is the one hue neither the ground nor the
# towers use — an enemy on grass and an enemy on path are equally visible,
# which matters because the path is where they always are.
#
 26  26  26	outline
 34  48  36	turf-0-shadow
 58  86  52	turf-1
 88 124  70	turf-2
124 164  92	turf-3-hilite
 76  56  38	path-0-shadow
118  90  60	path-1
158 128  88	path-2
196 170 128	path-3-hilite
 62  66  78	keep-0-shadow
104 110 124	keep-1
150 158 176	keep-2
206 214 232	keep-3-hilite
164  56  44	foe-0
214  92  60	foe-1
252 152  84	foe-2-hilite
